			(justify left bottom))
		(uuid "9e367257-390c-52e1-88bf-b6c9dc95c374"))
	(text "RX notes\n- RX antenna: Taoglas WDP.2458.25.4 25x25 mm pin-fed patch at the board centre (MagSafe enclosure).\n  Feed runs on B.Cu from the pin, then an RF via to L1. Pi match footprints for tuning.\n- The LNA now runs from 5V0 (QPL9547 recommended 3.15-5.25 V).\n- LNA is OFF at reset (100k pull-up on Shut_Down); firmware drives LNA_PD low to enable.\n- LNA supply through a ferrite bead from 5V0 (keeps buck ripple off the LNA).\n- RX OVERLOAD: TX carrier leaking into the RX antenna is in-band and gets ~17 dB of gain.\n  Keep antenna-to-antenna isolation >= 30 dB, or fit the pi pad (R_ATT shunts) so the\n  nRF ANT pin stays below 0 dBm (abs max +10 dBm). The nRF must never transmit: its ANT\n  pin drives straight into the LNA output.\n- All RF lines: 50 Ohm grounded CPW, see the PCB stackup notes."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 300 20 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27))
			(justify left top))
		(uuid "c6cf8b7f-db10-5b80-99f1-e74b31c6708a"))
	(symbol
		(lib_id "BEACON:Taoglas_WDP2458")
		(at 43.18 45.72 0)
